* Board 3, circuit 3: noise generator's filters (Fig. 9-8; R. A. Moog drawing 1431), as drawn,
* from the white noise follower Q4's emitter on. white: Q4's emitter; pink: Q3's collector (ahead
* of C20); red: Q6's collector (ahead of C28). The board's lower rail is -10 V (pins 17 / 18), not
* ground: drawing 1431 marks Q3's and Q6's collectors at +3.8 V.
.subckt noisefilters white pink red vp vn
* pink: R16 into the two RC branches and, through C1, Q3's base
r16 white p 10k
c3 p p3 0.12u
r8 p3 vn 3.3k
c2 p p2 0.033u
r13 p2 vn 220
c1 p b3 2.5u
* Q3: R3 3.3K load, R1 120 emitter, base biased from the collector through R6 / R7 560K,
* their middle decoupled by C4
q3 pink b3 e3 Q2N3392
r1 e3 vn 120
r3 vp pink 3.3k
r6 pink m 560k
r7 m b3 560k
c4 m vn 2.5u
* red: R12 10K into C7 .15 (106 Hz), C8 into Q6's base; Q6 a common emitter stage, R24 10K
* load, R15 3.9K emitter, base biased from the collector through R28 / R23 2.2M (middle
* decoupled by C10 .1), C22 .15 across the load (106 Hz again)
r12 pink r1n 10k
c7 r1n vn 0.15u
c8 r1n b6 2.5u
q6 red b6 e6 Q2N3392
r15 e6 vn 3.9k
r24 vp red 10k
c22 red vn 0.15u
r28 red m6 2.2meg
r23 m6 b6 2.2meg
c10 m6 vn 0.1u
.ends
